meta {
  name: Block
  type: http
  seq: 20
}

post {
  url: {{api}}/bonds/{{bondId}}/block
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "withdrawEntries": true
  }
}

docs {
  Ends the bond as Leave does, and the two of you cannot be paired again. 204, also on a bond that has already ended. Your partner is told nothing that a leave would not tell them.

  The body is required, and so is "withdrawEntries". As the example has it, true WITHDRAWS your entries: your partner stops reading them at once and the rows are erased within seconds. That cannot be undone. Set it to false to end the bond and leave what you wrote readable.

  With no body, {} or a null flag the answer is 400 MALFORMED_REQUEST and nothing is ended. Leave is different: there the flag is optional and the entries are kept unless asked to take them. A misspelt key is 400 and ends nothing.
}
